> ### **Understanding Interspecies Disease Transmission**
> Recent studies have uncovered evidence of MPXV transmission between fire-footed rope squirrels and sooty mangabeys, leading to an outbreak in Côte d’Ivoire. This discovery provides crucial insights into the mechanisms of zoonotic disease transmission and underscores the importance of monitoring wildlife for public health safety [82618]. 
> 
> Efforts to track such transmissions are vital not only for preventing potential outbreaks but also for preparing strategies that could mitigate the impacts of emerging infectious diseases on global biodiversity and human populations. Monitoring and research in wildlife disease ecology could be an essential first step toward building comprehensive biosecurity frameworks worldwide.
